Description: dual-script Korean/Japanese terminal font with Nerd Font icons
 Harena Term is a monospaced terminal typeface pairing an Iosevka-derived
 Latin design with CJK glyphs drawn primarily from Pretendard JP, laid out
 on a strict 1:2 Latin-to-CJK cell grid so Latin and East Asian text stay
 aligned in a terminal's character grid.
 .
 This package provides both regional cuts in a single install: the K face
 bakes Korean-preferred (ss05) glyph forms into its cmap, and the J face
 keeps the unmodified Pretendard JP forms; 537 hanja differ between them.
 Each cut ships in Regular and Bold weights, for four TrueType files in
 total.
 .
 The font also bundles glyph coverage from fourteen separately licensed
 Nerd Fonts icon sets (Material Design Icons, Font Awesome Free, Devicons,
 Codicons, Octicons, Weather Icons and others), giving terminal prompts,
 editors and other Powerline- or Nerd-Font-aware tools their expected icon
 glyphs.
